+## Round 2
+
+The gaps M5 found in the 2026-10-23 census (`docs/plans/2026-10-24-M5-truth.md` § Hardware round 2 candidates,
+`docs/research/2026-10-24-census-analysis.md` § What M5 could not answer). **About 14 minutes** with the optional
+steps left out (the table at the end adds them up). Nothing is sent to the One: only `tools/capture` runs, read-only.
+
+**Why by hand.** `tools/capture-session` walks a fixed list of 34 recordings (`tools/capture-session --list`: §6.1
+power-on to §6.7 strip search, plus the 8 extras) and has no option for another list, so none of these steps can be
+added to it. Each step is one `tools/capture --port 'Rane ONE MIDI 1' --seconds N --out <file>`. Mixxx, Serato and
+everything else that uses the One closed (exit 5 means something holds the port).
+
+Setup (1 min), once. The same as the census, except for what a step says: Stop Time at 12 o'clock on both decks,
+torque switch LOW, pitch faders at the centre detent, motors stopped, Shift not held.
+
+```
+D=captures/$(date +%F)-round2
+mkdir -p $D
+rec() { tools/capture --port 'Rane ONE MIDI 1' --seconds "$2" --out "$D/$1.jsonl"; }
+```
+
+`rec <name> <seconds>` starts at once and stops by itself; start it, then do the step. Say the step's timings out
+loud or watch a clock: every action below has a second count from the start of the recording, so the take itself
+carries the time. If a step goes wrong, `rm "$D/<name>.jsonl"` and run it again. Also take **one photo of each
+deck's section and of the front panel** now (no recording; the deck/layer buttons question, and the contour
+section's printed names).
+
+| # | Command | Do (seconds from the start) | Answers | Min |
+|--:|---------|-----------------------------|---------|----:|
+| 1 | `rec 01-fx-shift 60` | Hold **Shift** the whole time. 0–10 s: both FX paddles up and down (lever; it locks up). 10–30 s: FX1–FX6, one press each, 3 s apart. 30–40 s: the depth knob end to end. 40–50 s: the endless beat knob, a full turn each way. 50–58 s: Tap three times. | FX section with Shift (take 02 had none) | 1.2 |
+| 2 | `rec 02-play-d1 30` then `rec 03-play-d2 30` | Per deck, the motor starts at the first press: at 3 s press **Play**, hold 1 s, release; at 10 s **Shift+Play**, hold 1 s, release; at 20 s Play once more (stops it). | Play and Shift+Play in a census-style take (03/05 omitted Play) | 1.3 |
+| 3 | `rec 04-contour 60` | Motors stopped. 0–15 s deck 1 slow–fast knob from one end to the other, slowly; 15–30 s deck 2 the same; 30–36 s deck 1 reverse switch on, wait 3 s, off; 40–46 s deck 2 the same. Say (write down) the printed names of both knob ends and both switch positions. | The deck contour section (never touched) | 1.2 |
+| 4 | `rec 05-revpad-d1 30` then `rec 06-revpad-d2 30` | Per deck: 2 s Play (motor runs); 8 s the **reverse pad** (the deck pad that reversed deck 1 before take 18), 5 s, again at 14 s to turn it off; 22 s Play (stops). Deck 2: the same pad on deck 2. | Does the reverse pad send MIDI, and which message (take 15 started with `off ch5 10`) | 1.3 |
