+
+Each **Min** includes about 10 s to start the step. The nine steps add up to 13.3 min; with the 1 min setup the round
+is **14.3 min**.
+
+**Optional, not counted** (skip them if tired; each answers one thing the table leaves open):
+
+- 10. Replug: with the pitch fader of deck 1 well off-centre, unplug the One's USB, plug it in, and
+  `tools/capture --port 'Rane ONE MIDI 1' --wait 30 --seconds 20 --out $D/12-replug.jsonl` instead of `rec`. Does the
+  One report the fader before it moves (23/24 got nothing until it moved)? About 1 min.
+- 11. `rec 13-motor-off-mode 45`: Shift+Slip on deck 1 with the motor stopped (3 s), Play (8 s: does the platter stay
+  still, is note 0 still sent), turn the platter by hand a quarter turn (15 s), Play again (25 s), Shift+Slip again
+  (35 s). Take 25 never pressed Play in the mode. About 1 min.
+- 12. Deck 2's untouched motor: Play, 60 s, torque LOW, pitch centre (`rec 14-sag-d2 70`): does it sag again, down to
+  0.9755 as in take 21? If it does, swap the records/slipmats between the decks and repeat. About 1.5 min.
+
+Not in round 2: 45 rpm (the MK1 has no hardware switch; Serato sets it, D26) and anything that sends to the One.
+
+### After round 2: commit and report
+
+```
+ls $D | wc -l
+git add $D
+git commit -m "captures: $(date +%F)-round2 (<n> takes)"
+git push -u origin harness/rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24
+```
+
+In `.harness/runs/rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24/INBOX.md`, under `## Answers`, write: the session directory; which steps
+were skipped or redone, and why; and what only you can tell: (1) the printed names of the deck contour section and
+which end of each knob/switch you moved (step 3); (2) the reverse pad's name and where it is (step 4); (3) which pitch
+fader end is "top" and whether it is the `+` end (step 8); (4) the mismatching and `unknown` rows from step 9; (5)
+whether the One has any deck/layer buttons (photos); (6) what the platter did at torque HIGH compared with LOW (feel and
+sound: faster spin-up? harder to hold?); (7) anything odd.
