+- **D27 *default* · Mixxx's rate range is set to ±50 % (`rateRange` 0.5) on both decks, and M7 derives
+  `expectedRatio` from the raw pitch fader through `RaneOnePlatter.motorRatioFromFader`, read `FADER_LAG_MS` (35 ms)
+  late, not from `rate_ratio`.** The MK1's motor follows its own fader at 1 ± 0.5× (0 = 0.5×, 8192 = 1×, 16383 = 1.5×)
+  whatever Range is set to, and Range sends only note 43 (`captures/2026-10-23-census/23-pitch-d1.jsonl`,
+  `24-pitch-d2.jsonl`; `docs/research/2026-10-24-census-analysis.md` § Pitch fader and Range). Mixxx plays at
+  `rate_ratio = 1 + rate × rateRange × rate_dir` (inferred from its inverse in 2.5.6's `common-controller-scripts.js`
+  568–572; M6's Mixxx run checks it), and a mapping may set `rateRange` (2.5.6's Denon MC4000 and Traktor Kontrol S4
+  MK3 scripts do). So:
+  - **M6** sets `rateRange` 0.5 on `[Channel1]` and `[Channel2]` in `init` and maps the fader in script against the
+    **live** range: `rate = rate_dir × (motorRatioFromFader(v) − 1) / rateRange`, clamped to ±1, so `rate_ratio`
+    equals the motor's ratio whatever the user's slider-direction preference, and still does if Preferences, a skin
+    or a script changes `rateRange` to 0.5 or more. Below 0.5 the ends can't be reached and audio and platter part
+    company there: M6 logs it once (whether applying Preferences resets `rateRange` is UNVERIFIED; M6's Mixxx run
+    checks). **The pitch fader gets no soft takeover** (the motor follows the fader at once; a Mixxx rate waiting for
+    pick-up would disagree with the platter). The Range button is not mapped to `rateRange` (it changes nothing on
+    the motor); what else it does is M6's call.
+  - **The fader's position is unknown until it moves.** The One sends it in the power-on dump (01: 8192 on both decks)
+    but not when a port opens (23 and 24 have none until 11.5 and 8.4 s). Until the first CC 9/41 of a deck, M6 leaves
+    Mixxx's `rate` alone and M7 takes the centre (8192) as the motor's speed, as `faderExpected` does. If the fader is
+    elsewhere, an untouched platter reads as a hand and goes to platter control, which plays at the record's real
+    speed, the fader's: the music is right, only the switch-over is off until the fader moves. Round 2: does anything make the One
+    report its fader (a replug, Shift)?
+  - **M7** passes `motorRatioFromFader(fader value FADER_LAG_MS ago)` (0 with the motor off) as the state machine's
+    `expectedRatio`, and Mixxx's `rate_ratio` as its `playRatio`. `FADER_LAG_MS` 35 is a DEFAULTS key and a D25-style
+    user setting: on take 23, read now there is one takeover from the lag alone and a 10 ms deviation of 3.79 %
+    against `TAKEOVER_TOL` 3 %; 25 ms late 0 and 2.28 %; 35 ms 0 and 1.65 % (the estimator follows the fader 35 ms
+    behind on deck 1, 55 ms on deck 2). `RETARGET_MS` stays 0 (it removes a takeover at one delay only). The motors'
