+    moving the motor, and the core would then read an untouched platter as a hand. With the raw fader those still
+    show (the clock plays at `playRatio`, the platter at the motor's speed), but the switch-over isn't fooled by them.
+    How Sync and hybrid playback coexist is M7's (open).
+  - **Not covered:** deck 2 at the slow end runs 2–9 % under its target (torque LOW), so below the centre it hands
+    over to the platter 6 times in take 24 at 35 ms (5–7 at 0–50 ms); D25's `TAKEOVER_TOL` is the knob, round 2's
+    torque HIGH take the test. Fast fader moves are not in the takes (≤ 0.074 of ratio per 100 ms), so 35 ms's
+    margin on a slam is UNVERIFIED (round 2).
