+  direction (`sign(e) · ratio` against `BACKSPIN_RATIO`/`BACKSPIN_EXIT_RATIO`), and D24's stall absorption works
+  along the clock's direction at the takeover. Every other rule already used `|ratio|` or `ratio / e`. Mirrored
+  input (ratio, expectedRatio, playRatio and ticks negated) gives the same states and control and the negated
+  position, on census 18 (backspin), 31 (hold), 23 (the fader, with `RETARGET_MS` 200) and a D24 stall
+  (`tests/platter-state.test.mjs` "D29: …", red before). `tools/platter-run --expected` takes a negative ratio.
+  Why: deck 1's reverse pad was on through takes 15 and 17 (Michael's note on 18), so the motor ran backwards at
+  speed for 60 s (`captures/2026-10-23-census/15-motor-d1-33.jsonl` −0.9995, M5-05). With `expectedRatio` +1 the
+  core read that as a backspin and kept the platter in control the whole take. With −1 from the Play press, 15
