+  the glue learns the direction (the pad's note 16 is UNVERIFIED, round 2; or Mixxx's `reverse` control) and
+  whether Mixxx should follow the One's reverse at all are M7's. Risk: expectedRatio flipping from +1 straight to −1 at speed (reverse pressed while
+  playing) hands the deck to the platter on that update as `backspin` (T1, no `TAKEOVER_MS` wait), then
+  scratching/held while the motor turns round, and back to `motor_at_speed` about 0.75 s later in a scripted flip;
+  no flip under 20 ms, but `SPINUP_MS` isn't re-armed by a sign change (unpinned either way). D24's direction is
+  the clock's (`playRatio`'s sign), which only differs from expectedRatio's if the glue makes it so (unpinned). To undo:
