+# M5 plan · Truth (2026-10-24)
+
+Goal (spec §5 M5, Michael's brief for run `rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24`): check the M4 platter core against
+Michael's capture session `captures/2026-10-23-census/` (34 takes, his per-take notes in its `README.md`), correct
+the decoder and the constants test-first where the takes disagree, answer spec §5 M5's questions and its seven open
+questions from cited takes or mark them UNVERIFIED with the reason, and write the census into the MK1 control map.
+This plan only maps questions to takes, commands and destinations. M5-02..M5-10 build and measure.
+
+Build-only, and nothing is sent to the One: every M5 command reads files under `captures/`. No Mixxx runs in M5.
+
+- **Analysis document:** `docs/research/2026-10-24-census-analysis.md` (modelled on
+  `docs/research/2026-10-19-quick-capture-analysis.md`). Every number in it names its take and the command that
+  printed it, so M5-10's reviewer can re-run it. Sections, in this order: `Census`, `Power-on dump`,
+  `Platter format`, `Motor`, `Shift+Slip and Stop Time`, `Pitch fader and Range`, `Strip search`,
+  `Other deck's stray pairs`, `Platter runs`, `Not data`, `What M5 could not answer`.
+- **Decisions from this plan:** D1 settled in place (hybrid, Michael 2026-10-24), **D25** (configurable
+  switch-over, Michael's requirement) and **D26 *default*** (33⅓ only; 45 rpm needs a host motor command no capture
+  shows). Next free number after this plan: **D27**.
+- **Setup of the whole session** (README): Stop Time at 12 o'clock on both decks, torque LOW. Torque HIGH was never
+  captured; any number below is "at torque LOW" and says so.
+- **Deck 1's reverse pad** was ON for every deck 1 motor take before 18 (Michael's note on take 18). Takes 15 and
+  17 run backwards and are used as mirrored-direction data. Hand takes (07–11) are not affected.
+
+### First look (plan-time peek, 2026-10-24; hints only, re-derive and cite in the feature that uses them)
+
+A one-off Node count of `type ch d1` per take (and every message that isn't CC 6 or pitch bend, with its time):
+- The platter is CC 6 + pitch bend on channel 1 in 07–11, 15–20, 23, 25 and on channel 2 in 12–14, 21, 22, 24,
+  29–34. Takes 11 and 30 (alt jog) are hand turns with Shift (note 50 ch 16) held about 10 s: nothing new.
+- Touch takes 10 (12 messages) and 14 (6) hold only CC 6/pitch bend pairs: 6 pairs (CC 6 71 → 66, 5 ticks) and 3 pairs
+  (19 → 21, 2 ticks), no other message. So far, no touch message.
+- Note 0 on the deck's channel (Play, the guess) has an on/off at 1.77 s (15), 2.10 s (21), 1.98 s (24), 2.23 s (20)
+  and 1.78 s (34); in the stop takes 20 and 34 that press may be the stop, before the CC 72 sweep. 19 and 33 show
+  no note 0 among their first 14 non-platter messages.
+  Take 17 starts with an `off ch1 0` at 0.00 s and 31 with on/off at 0.00 s (pressed as recording started).
+- **The Stop Time knob sends MIDI:** CC 72 on the deck's channel sweeps in 19 and 33 (down from 58/60) and 20 and
+  34 (up from 1).
+- Take 23 has exactly two Range presses (note 43 ch 1, on/off each) and the 14-bit fader CC 9/41 on ch 1 (4,476
+  pairs, CC 9 first); no other non-platter message. 24 likewise on ch 2.
+- Take 25: four Shift presses; Shift + note 10 on ch 5 twice (deck 1) and on ch 6 twice (deck 2); `cc ch15 96`
+  twice; Play ch 1 twice. Take 15 starts with an `off ch5 10` at 0.00 s.
