+## Motor
+
+Written by M5-05. Commands are `tools/platter-windows <take> [--deck 2] --from <s> --to <s> --window-ms <ms>
+[--cross <ratio>,…]` (new in M5-05: the core's decoder, estimator and state machine over fixed host-time windows,
+and the first estimator update past each `--cross` threshold after `--from`), `tools/analyze-platter` and
+`tools/platter-run`; the take is `captures/2026-10-23-census/<take>`. A **ratio** is the platter's speed over 33⅓
+rpm at 3600 ticks/rev (2000 ticks/s), signed: backward is negative. **Device ratio** counts only timed deltas (−1/−2
+markers left out); **host ratio** is net ticks over host seconds. Everything here is at **torque LOW** and, unless a
+take moves it, the pitch fader at its centre: every fader move in the census ends at exactly 8192 (CC 9 = 64, CC 41
+= 0; last messages of 03, 05, 23 and 24 in `tools/take-events <take>`), and the power-on dump reports 8192 on both
+decks (01 at 1.999 s). Torque HIGH was never captured against a hand (take 25 flips it only while deck 1 spins
+freely: § Shift+Slip and Stop Time). Nothing was sent to the One.
+
